# Auto-commit Exp work

This workspace overrides “only commit when asked” **and** the six-step status/diff/log/HEREDOC protocol. Git is ~40ms here; the delay is extra Shell round-trips and PowerShell HEREDOC retries. Do not push. Do not promote.

## Where

| Edits in | Commit in | Branch |
|---|---|---|
| `F:\Mikes-UI-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |
| `F:\Mikes-HALO-Jump-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |
| `F:\Mikes-Invade-and-Annex-Exp` | that folder | `experimental` |

Never `git checkout experimental` in a production folder. Never commit `addon.gproj`. Skip `resourceDatabase.rdb`.

## How

**One Shell call per repo.** Do not run `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, or a separate `git commit`. Do not nest `powershell -File` (this shell is already PowerShell). If several repos changed, invoke the script in parallel.

```
& "F:\Mikes-Invade-and-Annex\tools\Commit-Experimental.ps1" -Repo "F:\Mikes-UI-Exp" -Message "Why sentence." -Files path/a.c, path/b.md
```

Message: 1–2 sentences on **why**, not a file list. Pass the files you edited this turn. If the script prints `SKIPPED`, stop.

Do not commit production addon scripts. Cursor rules, skills, and `tools\` under I&A may be committed in the folder you actually edited (production I&A is limited to `.cursor/` and `tools/`).
